<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Discovery and intelligence"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/research-services/product-development/"}>{"Discovery & intelligence"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l is-scroll"}> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/product-development/clinical-trial-support/"}>{"Clinical trial support"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/literature-review-and-gap/"}>{"Literature review & gap"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/evidence-gap-map/"}>{"Evidence gap map"}</a></li> <li><a href={"/services/research-services/experimental-design/"}>{"Study design"}</a></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Scope the question "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/research-services/product-development/"}>{"Discovery & intelligence"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Clinical trial support"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Clinical Trial Support"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p><b>{"The paperwork is where trials actually fail."}</b>{" Not the science — the protocol that had to be amended three times, the consent form nobody could read, the statistical plan written after the data arrived, the results record that missed its deadline. Pubrica’s clinical trial writers and biostatisticians build the documentation and the evidence layer of a clinical trial: protocol, investigator’s brochure, consent form, statistical analysis plan, study report, registry records and the manuscript at the end. "}<b>{"We do not monitor sites, manage patients or hold sponsor obligations"}</b>{" — you remain the sponsor throughout, and that is stated here rather than discovered later."}</p> <ul className={"hpts"}> <li><b>{"Protocol authoring to ICH M11"}</b>{", the harmonised structured template adopted at Step 4 in November 2025 — which most templates in circulation still predate"}</li> <li><b>{"Statistical analysis plans with the estimand framed first"}</b>{" under ICH E9(R1), because deciding how intercurrent events are handled after unblinding is not a statistical decision any more"}</li> <li><b>{"Clinical study reports to ICH E3"}</b>{", full, abbreviated or synoptic, with patient narratives and integrated summaries written from your locked dataset"}</li> <li><b>{"Registry disclosure that meets the deadline"}</b>{" — ClinicalTrials.gov, CTIS and CTRI records drafted and filed on your account, under your responsible party"}</li> <li><b>{"Documentation, evidence and analysis only."}</b>{" No monitoring, no site management, no sponsor obligation accepted in writing — the boundary is the first thing on this page because it is the thing buyers most often find out too late"}</li> </ul> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#cts-sample"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"What clinical trial support covers"}</b></span> <span>{"And what it deliberately does not"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Protocol, IB, ICF and CSR authoring"}</b><span>{"Included"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"SAP, estimands and independent analysis"}</b><span>{"Included"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Registry records and results disclosure"}</b><span>{"On your account"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"TMF structure and inspection readiness"}</b><span>{"Reviewed, not held"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Site monitoring, SDV and site management"}</b><span>{"A registered CRO only"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "3%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Sponsor obligations under 21 CFR 312.52"}</b><span>{"They stay with you"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "2%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Design"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" documented "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" registered "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" analysed "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"reported"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every document"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Built to the current ICH version"}</li> <li>{"Traceable to the protocol"}</li> <li>{"Reviewed by a trial methodologist"}</li> <li>{"Deadline dated on the order"}</li> <li>{"Revisions included, not charged"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i proof__i--ask"}><b>{"Quoted per project"}</b><span>{"On phase, document set and therapeutic area"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"By deliverable"}</b><span>{"Protocol, SAP, CSR and disclosure priced separately"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ICH E6(R3), M11, E3 and E9(R1)"}</b><span>{"ISO 14155:2026 for device trials"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-what-we-do-ilxl2o"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-who-we-serve-1w42ary"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-our-compliance-1iff9cb"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-how-it-works-18yje18"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-our-experts-yugvix"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#cts-sample"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-packages-e13it8"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-guarantee-1av9hzt"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-client-stories-djyp7k"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-clinical-trial-support-faq-1ng8kvb"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-what-we-do-ilxl2o"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What you get"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six things, on every trial engagement."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"One protocol, one named set of regulators and registries. What your ethics approval and your registration commit you to bounds everything downstream."}</p> </div> </div> <div data-smpls={""} className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"A protocol built to the current template"}</b> <span>{"ICH M11 structured protocol content, adopted at Step 4 in November 2025, with critical-to-quality factors identified under ICH E8(R1) rather than every procedure treated as equally important."}</span> <p className={"smpl"} data-smpl={""}><span className={"smpl__k"}>{"From the protocol review"}</span><del>{"Schedule of assessments: 41 procedures per visit, all listed as required."}</del><ins>{"Twelve procedures traced to no objective and removed. Tufts data published in December 2025 puts roughly a third of Phase III procedures as non-core, carrying 25 to 30 per cent of participant and site burden."}</ins></p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Eligibility criteria that can actually recruit"}</b> <span>{"Each criterion tested against the population it excludes, because criteria accumulate silently and under-enrolment is the single largest non-scientific reason trials terminate."}</span> <p className={"smpl smpl--x"} data-smpl={""}><span className={"smpl__k"}>{"From the feasibility analysis"}</span><ins>{"Four criteria excluded 61% of the eligible population between them, and two of the four were traceable to a previous protocol rather than to this study’s question. Of terminated trials with posted results, 39% stopped for insufficient accrual."}</ins></p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"A statistical analysis plan with the estimand first"}</b> <span>{"Population, variable, intercurrent event handling and summary measure defined under ICH E9(R1) before the data exists — which is the only point at which the decision is still a scientific one."}</span> <p className={"smpl"} data-smpl={""}><span className={"smpl__k"}>{"From the SAP"}</span><del>{"Missing data will be handled using last observation carried forward."}</del><ins>{"Treatment policy estimand; intercurrent events specified as treatment discontinuation and rescue medication, each with its handling strategy stated; sensitivity analyses named. Written before unblinding, which is what makes it defensible."}</ins></p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"A consent form a participant can read"}</b> <span>{"Plain language at the reading level your ethics committee requires, with the risks stated where they will be seen. Informed consent is a recurring category in FDA clinical investigator inspection findings."}</span> <p className={"smpl"} data-smpl={""}><span className={"smpl__k"}>{"From the ICF"}</span><del>{"You may experience adverse sequelae including but not limited to hepatic dysfunction."}</del><ins>{"Some people taking this drug have had liver problems. We will test your liver with a blood test at every visit. If the test changes, we will stop the study drug. Same information, at a reading age people actually have."}</ins></p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"A study report to ICH E3"}</b> <span>{"Full, abbreviated or synoptic, with patient narratives, integrated summaries and Module 2.5 and 2.7 content written from the locked dataset rather than from the top-line tables."}</span> <p className={"smpl smpl--x"} data-smpl={""}><span className={"smpl__k"}>{"From the CSR"}</span><ins>{"Efficacy section written against the pre-specified estimand, with every deviation from the SAP listed and dated in section 9.8. A CSR that quietly reanalyses is the one an inspector reads twice."}</ins></p> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Disclosure that lands before the deadline"}</b> <span>{"ClinicalTrials.gov, CTIS and CTRI records drafted and filed on your account. Registration within 21 days of first enrolment, results within 12 months of primary completion."}</span> <p className={"smpl smpl--x"} data-smpl={""}><span className={"smpl__k"}>{"From the disclosure log"}</span><ins>{"Across 10,605 applicable trials, only 37.2% met the 12-month results requirement — 73.7% for industry sponsors but 25.5% for academic ones. Small sponsors were the least compliant, and FDA has begun issuing notices of noncompliance."}</ins></p> </div> </div> <p className={"smpln rv rv-d2"}>{"Samples are taken from real jobs, with the client, the field and anything identifying changed. Hover any one of them to play it again."}</p> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Trial support by deliverable"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Twelve deliverables, bought together or one at a time."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Most sponsors start with one document and come back. Each is quoted on its own, and the packages below are simply the combinations that recur."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"etypes rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Clinical development plan and target product profile"}</b><span>{"The multi-study roadmap and the label claims written as a specification, so the trials are designed backwards from what you intend to be able to say."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Protocol and protocol synopsis"}</b><span>{"Full protocol to ICH M11 structure, plus the synopsis, with critical-to-quality factors identified under E8(R1) rather than every procedure weighted equally."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Protocol amendments and change-impact documentation"}</b><span>{"Substantial and non-substantial amendments drafted with the rationale, the affected sections and the re-consent implication set out for the ethics committee."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Investigator’s brochure and annual updates"}</b><span>{"The IB authored from the nonclinical and clinical data package, and the annual update that most sponsors discover is overdue."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Informed consent and assent forms"}</b><span>{"Master ICF, site-specific versions, assent and re-consent forms, written in plain language at the reading level the ethics committee requires."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"CRF specification and annotated CRF"}</b><span>{"The case report form designed against the analysis plan and the annotated CRF mapped to CDISC domains — the specification, for your data management team to build from."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Statistical analysis plan and sample size"}</b><span>{"Estimands framed under E9(R1), power and sample size calculation, randomisation schedule specification and the analysis populations defined before the database locks."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Independent analysis and TLF production"}</b><span>{"Analysis against your locked dataset with tables, listings and figures, plus SDTM and ADaM dataset specification and reviewer’s guides where a submission is the destination."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Clinical study report and narratives"}</b><span>{"ICH E3 full, abbreviated or synoptic CSRs, patient narratives for deaths, serious adverse events and discontinuations, integrated summaries of safety and efficacy, and Module 2.5 and 2.7 content."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Registration, results disclosure and lay summaries"}</b><span>{"ClinicalTrials.gov, CTIS and CTRI records drafted and filed on your account, results records to deadline, and EU CTR Annex V plain-language summaries."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Trial master file and inspection readiness"}</b><span>{"TMF structure against the DIA reference model, completeness review, and a gap analysis against the finding categories inspectors actually record."}</span></div> <div className={"etype"}><b>{"Publication planning and manuscripts"}</b><span>{"Publication plan, manuscripts to CONSORT 2025, abstracts, posters and congress materials, under GPP 2022 and the ICMJE authorship criteria."}</span></div> </div> <p className={"smpln rv rv-d2"}><b>{"The boundary, stated plainly."}</b>{" Everything above is documentation, analysis and evidence: you sign it, you own it, you submit it, and you remain the sponsor. We do not monitor sites, manage or recruit patients, handle investigational product, operate a safety database of record, or accept a written transfer of sponsor obligations under 21 CFR 312.52. Those require a contracted CRO — and in India, an organisation registered with CDSCO under Chapter VA of the amended rules, mandatory since April 2025. Where you need that, we will say so and work alongside whoever holds it."}</p> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-who-we-serve-1w42ary"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Seven kinds of sponsor, one documentation standard."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"What changes is which regulator, which registry and which reporting guideline applies. What does not change is that you remain the sponsor and we write to the current version."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Academic and investigator-initiated trials"}</b><span>{"Where the principal investigator holds both sponsor and investigator obligations with no clinical operations department behind them. Academic sponsors met the 12-month results requirement 25.5% of the time against 73.7% for industry — the sharpest quantified gap in the field, and the easiest to close."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Biotech without internal clinical operations"}</b><span>{"Where the first protocol is written under board pressure and becomes the most expensive document in the programme. Design review before ethics submission is worth more here than anywhere else."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Mid-size pharmaceutical companies"}</b><span>{"Where clinical operations exist but not at portfolio scale, and medical and regulatory writing capacity is bought in per document or on a retained basis."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Medical device manufacturers"}</b><span>{"Governed by 21 CFR 812, EU MDR 2017/745 and ISO 14155 rather than by ICH E6 alone — and currently re-papering clinical investigation plans against the 2026 fourth edition, since the 2020 version is withdrawn."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Contract research organisations"}</b><span>{"Buying overflow writing, biostatistics and disclosure capacity as a subcontractor. Note that under E6(R3), sponsor oversight now reaches work a CRO further subcontracts."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Hospitals and academic medical centres"}</b><span>{"Running sites rather than sponsoring: source documentation practice, deviation management, essential document completeness and inspection readiness against the categories inspectors actually record."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "6" }}><b>{"Nutraceutical and supplement companies running human studies"}</b><span>{"Where the pivotal question is whether an IND is needed at all, and that turns on the claim: a structure-function claim generally does not require one, a disease claim generally does. Getting that determination wrong is the expensive error in this segment."}</span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-our-compliance-1iff9cb"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Seven references, and most of them changed recently."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"This is a field where out-of-date citation is the norm. Everything below is the current designation as at September 2026, and the page is re-checked when a version moves."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds stds--7"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"GCP"}>{"ICH"}<em>{"E6(R3)"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICH Good Clinical Practice "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(E6(R3), not E6(R2))"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Principles and Annex 1 reached Step 4 in January 2025 and took effect in the EU in July 2025; Annex 2, covering pragmatic and decentralised designs, takes effect January 2027. Delegating a task does not delegate accountability, and oversight now extends to subcontracted work."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Protocol"}>{"ICH"}<em>{"M11"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICH M11 structured protocol "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(Step 4, November 2025)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The harmonised protocol template and technical specification, known as CeSHarP. TransCelerate has realigned its Common Protocol Template to it. Most templates still in circulation predate it."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Reports"}>{"ICH"}<em>{"E3"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICH E3 clinical study reports "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(with Q&A (R1), 2012)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The structure and content of a CSR. Manuscripts are written to CONSORT 2025 and protocols to SPIRIT 2025 — both replaced the 2010 and 2013 versions last year — under the 2024 revision of the Declaration of Helsinki and GPP 2022."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Statistics"}>{"ICH"}<em>{"E9(R1)"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICH E9 with the estimands addendum "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(E9(R1), 2019)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The estimand framework. Citing E9 alone is now incomplete: the addendum is what governs how intercurrent events are defined and handled, and it has to be settled before the data exists."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Devices"}>{"ISO"}<em>{"14155:2026"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ISO 14155 clinical investigation of devices "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(4th edition, March 2026)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"The 2020 edition is withdrawn. Device sponsors are re-papering investigation plans and SOPs against the fourth edition now, alongside EU MDR 2017/745 and 21 CFR 812."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Disclosure"}>{"REG"}<em>{"registries"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Registration and results disclosure "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(FDAAA 801, EU CTR 536/2014, CTRI)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Registration within 21 days of first enrolment and results within 12 months of primary completion under FDAAA 801; CTIS rather than EudraCT for EU trials, with Annex V lay summaries; prospective CTRI registration in India."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ISO 9001"}>{"ISO"}<em>{"9001:2015"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"Quality management "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"How the documents are drafted, reviewed, versioned and released — which is what an audit of the writing function actually looks at."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"An inspector asks who decided, not what tool was used."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Trial documentation is read by people whose job is to trace decisions. That makes provenance the constraint rather than speed — every protocol decision has to be attributable to a person and defensible on the day somebody asks."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Consistency checking across a document set. Finding precedent language and prior protocol versions. Drafting highly templated sections a writer then verifies against source."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Eligibility criteria, endpoints or estimands; safety language; anything in a submission as drafted; and any decision an inspector would expect to trace to a named individual."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-how-it-works-18yje18"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How clinical trial support works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Five steps, and the first one is worth the most."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Almost everything expensive in a trial is decided in the protocol. After ethics approval, changing it costs a median of six figures and most of a year."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step one"}</span> <h3>{"Design review and document planning"}</h3> <p>{"We read the protocol or synopsis against what it commits you to: the recruitable population, the endpoints and their estimands, the procedures that map to no objective, and the registries and regulators the geography pulls in."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step two"}</span> <h3>{"Core document authoring"}</h3> <p>{"Protocol to ICH M11, investigator’s brochure, informed consent form in plain language, CRF specification and annotated CRF, and the statistical analysis plan with the estimand framed before the database is built."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step three"}</span> <h3>{"Registration and ethics package"}</h3> <p>{"Registry records drafted and filed on your account — ClinicalTrials.gov, CTIS or CTRI — prospectively, alongside the ethics and regulatory submission package for your signature."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step four"}</span> <h3>{"Analysis and reporting"}</h3> <p>{"Independent statistical analysis against your locked dataset, tables, listings and figures, then the clinical study report to ICH E3 with patient narratives and integrated summaries."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Step five"}</span> <h3>{"Disclosure, publication and inspection readiness"}</h3> <p>{"Results records posted to deadline, lay summaries where the EU CTR requires them, the manuscript written to CONSORT 2025, and a trial master file completeness and inspection-readiness review."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send the protocol. We will run the amendment risk check free."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"A read of your draft protocol for the things that generate amendments later — eligibility criteria that will not recruit, endpoints with no matching estimand, procedures that are not core to any objective. Phase II protocols now average 3.3 substantial amendments and Phase III 3.5, and the cheapest one to avoid is the first. Five business days, no charge."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#/pricing"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The protocol"}</b><span>{"Draft or synopsis"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The phase"}</b><span>{"And the indication"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The endpoints"}</b><span>{"Primary and secondary"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The geography"}</b><span>{"Which regulators and registries"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Product type"}</b><span>{"Drug, biologic, device or supplement"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The deadline"}</b><span>{"And the first-patient-in date"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"Send it before ethics submission. Getz’s 2023 dataset puts 260 days between identifying the need for an amendment and final ethics approval, with sites running different protocol versions for 215 of them. Every hour spent on the protocol now is bought back several times over."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div></section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-our-experts-yugvix"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section id={"cts-sample"} className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"One protocol section, as drafted and as issued."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Play the changes through one at a time. Same study, same science — one version generates amendments and the other does not."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"mkup rv rv-d1 is-after"} data-mkup={""}> <div className={"mkup__bar"}> <div className={"mkup__seg"} role={"group"} aria-label={"Which version to show"}> <button type={"button"} className={"mkup__sb"} data-mk-state={"before"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"As drafted"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"mkup__sb"} data-mk-state={"after"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"As issued"}</button> </div> <button type={"button"} className={"mkup__play"} data-mk-play={""}><i aria-hidden={"true"} />{"Play the changes"}</button> <p className={"mkup__count"} data-mk-count={""}><b>{"6"}</b>{" changes, each explained"}</p> </div> <div className={"mkup__pane"} id={"cts-p1"}> <div className={"mkup__ba"}> <div className={"mkup__v mkup__v--b"}> <p className={"mkup__cap"}><b>{"As drafted."}</b>{" An investigator’s Phase II protocol, pre-ethics submission."}</p> <ul className={"mkln mkln--b"}> <li>{"18 eligibility criteria, 6 carried from a previous study"}</li> <li>{"41 procedures per visit, all “required”"}</li> <li>{"“Missing data handled by last observation carried forward”"}</li> <li>{"Three co-primary endpoints"}</li> <li>{"“Adverse sequelae including hepatic dysfunction” in the ICF"}</li> <li>{"Registration “after first patient enrolled”"}</li> <li>{"2013 template, ICH E6(R2) referenced throughout"}</li> </ul> </div> <div className={"mkup__v mkup__v--a"}> <p className={"mkup__cap"}><b>{"As issued."}</b>{" The same study, after the amendment risk check."}</p> <ul className={"mkln"}> <li>{"13 criteria "}<em>{"— four excluded 61% of the eligible population between them"}</em></li> <li>{"29 procedures "}<em>{"— twelve traced to no objective and removed"}</em></li> <li>{"Treatment policy estimand, intercurrent events named with handling strategies"}</li> <li>{"One primary, two key secondary "}<em>{"— multiplicity controlled, not assumed"}</em></li> <li>{"“Some people taking this drug have had liver problems”"}</li> <li>{"Prospective, within 21 days of first enrolment, deadline on the plan"}</li> <li>{"ICH M11 structure, E6(R3) and E9(R1) referenced"}</li> </ul> <p className={"mkup__fn"}>{"Illustrative; the indication, the criteria and the figures are changed. The pattern is the one most investigator-drafted protocols follow."}</p> </div> </div> <aside className={"mkup__notes"}> <p className={"mkup__note"} style={{ transitionDelay: "0ms" }}><b><i>{"1"}</i>{"Eligibility criteria accumulate by inheritance"}</b>{"Six of the eighteen came from a previous protocol rather than from this study’s question. Nobody adds a criterion intending to halve recruitment, which is exactly how it happens."}</p> <p className={"mkup__note"} style={{ transitionDelay: "0ms" }}><b><i>{"2"}</i>{"A third of the schedule is usually not core"}</b>{"Tufts analysis published in December 2025 found roughly a third of Phase III procedures non-core, carrying 25 to 30 per cent of the burden on participants and sites — and Phase III protocols now collect an average of 5.9 million datapoints."}</p> <p className={"mkup__note"} style={{ transitionDelay: "0ms" }}><b><i>{"3"}</i>{"The estimand is a design decision, not an analysis one"}</b>{"Deciding how discontinuation and rescue medication are handled after you have seen the data is not statistics. E9(R1) exists because that used to be normal."}</p> <p className={"mkup__note"} style={{ transitionDelay: "0ms" }}><b><i>{"4"}</i>{"Three co-primary endpoints is a multiplicity problem"}</b>{"Either the alpha is split and the study is underpowered, or it is not and the result will not survive review. One primary and two key secondary endpoints is a decision; three co-primaries is usually an unresolved argument."}</p> <p className={"mkup__note"} style={{ transitionDelay: "0ms" }}><b><i>{"5"}</i>{"The consent form is read by the participant, not by the committee"}</b>{"Informed consent is a recurring FDA clinical investigator inspection finding. Writing it at the reading age people actually have is a protection for the trial as much as for them."}</p> <p className={"mkup__note"} style={{ transitionDelay: "0ms" }}><b><i>{"6"}</i>{"Registration is prospective or it is a problem"}</b>{"Within 21 days of first enrolment under FDAAA 801, and before the first participant under ICMJE — which means a retrospective registration can cost you the publication as well as the compliance record."}</p> </aside> <div className={"mkup__foot"}><span>{"Illustrative · indication and values changed"}</span><span>{"Comprehensive package · Phase II, single region"}</span></div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Benefits of getting the documentation right"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Where the money and the months actually go."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Each of these is a documented failure mode with a cost attached, not a claim about how much faster your trial will run."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}> <span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span> <span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Fewer amendments, which is where the cost is"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Phase II protocols now average 3.3 substantial amendments and Phase III 3.5, with 260 days from identifying the need to final ethics approval. The 2016 Tufts costing put the median direct cost at $141,000 in Phase II and $535,000 in Phase III."}</span></span> </div> <div className={"ben"}> <span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span> <span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Sites stop running different protocol versions"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"In the same 2023 dataset, sites operated under different versions simultaneously for an average of 215 days per amendment, with two-thirds of participants re-consented. Every one of those days is a deviation risk."}</span></span> </div> <div className={"ben"}> <span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span> <span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Start-up that does not drift"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"A 2025 study of 308 site activations found a median of 133 days from go-live to activation with a lean start-up workflow, against 277 days without one. The documentation package is most of what sits on that path."}</span></span> </div> <div className={"ben"}> <span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span> <span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The disclosure deadline gets met"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Only 37.2% of applicable trials met the 12-month results requirement, and 25.5% among academic sponsors. FDA has moved from pre-notice letters to notices of noncompliance."}</span></span> </div> <div className={"ben"}> <span className={"ben__n"}>{"05"}</span> <span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Inspection findings land in the low categories"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The EMA GCP inspectors recorded 720 deficiencies across 67 inspections in 2023, 36 of them critical, with 40% in the general category — essential documents, training records and source documentation."}</span></span> </div> <div className={"ben"}> <span className={"ben__n"}>{"06"}</span> <span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The publication is not the bottleneck"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"CONSORT 2025 compliance, the trial registration number, the protocol and SAP as supplements, and the deviations already documented. A manuscript written from a complete CSR is a different piece of work from one written from memory."}</span></span> </div> </div> </div> </section><section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-packages-e13it8"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Scope and quote"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Four packages, all quoted."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Cost turns on the phase, the document set, the therapeutic area and the number of regulators and registries in scope. Nobody in this market publishes rates, and a page that did would be quoting a number it could not hold."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers tiers--4 rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Starter"}</span> <h3>{"Starter package"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Investigator-initiated trials and single-document needs"}</p> <p className={"tier__price tier__price--ask"}><b>{"Quoted per project"}</b><span>{"On the document and the therapeutic area"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"By deliverable"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"One core document: protocol, ICF, SAP or CSR"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Written to the current ICH structure for that document"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Registry record drafted and filed on your account"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"One revision round"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Delivered in editable Word with a version history"}</span></li></ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Where most academic sponsors start, and usually with the protocol or the CSR."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#cts-sample"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/?service=Clinical+Trial+Support&package=Starter+package&subject=Quote+request%3A+Clinical+Trial+Support+%E2%80%94+Starter+package"}>{"Request a quote"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Advanced"}</span> <h3>{"Advanced package"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Biotech and device sponsors running a first trial"}</p> <p className={"tier__price tier__price--ask"}><b>{"Quoted per project"}</b><span>{"On phase, document count and geography"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"By scope"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Protocol to ICH M11 with synopsis"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Investigator’s brochure and informed consent form"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"CRF specification and annotated CRF"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Statistical analysis plan with estimands framed under E9(R1)"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Registration record drafted and filed prospectively"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Amendment risk review before ethics submission"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Two revision rounds per document"}</span></li></ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"The document set a first trial needs before it can open. Device trials are built to ISO 14155:2026 rather than to E6 alone."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#cts-sample"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/?service=Clinical+Trial+Support&package=Advanced+package&subject=Quote+request%3A+Clinical+Trial+Support+%E2%80%94+Advanced+package"}>{"Request a quote"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Comprehensive"}</span> <h3>{"Comprehensive package"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Sponsors taking a trial from design through to publication"}</p> <p className={"tier__price tier__price--ask"}><b>{"Quoted per project"}</b><span>{"On phase, registries and submission destination"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"By scope"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Advanced"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Independent analysis against your locked dataset, with TLFs"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Clinical study report to ICH E3 with patient narratives"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Integrated summaries and Module 2.5 and 2.7 content"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Results disclosure to deadline, with EU CTR lay summaries"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"TMF completeness and inspection-readiness review"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Manuscript to CONSORT 2025 with the registration number carried through"}</span></li></ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Where a regulatory submission is the destination, say so — the dataset specifications and the reviewer’s guides change."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#cts-sample"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/?service=Clinical+Trial+Support&package=Comprehensive+package&subject=Quote+request%3A+Clinical+Trial+Support+%E2%80%94+Comprehensive+package"}>{"Request a quote"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Custom"}</span> <h3>{"Custom and ongoing"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"CROs subcontracting, and sponsors with a recurring disclosure obligation"}</p> <p className={"tier__price tier__price--ask"}><b>{"Quoted per project"}</b><span>{"On volume and the obligation being covered"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"By arrangement"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Disclosure managed as a standing obligation across a portfolio"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Overflow medical and regulatory writing on a retained basis"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Standards transition mapping — E6(R2) to E6(R3), ISO 14155:2020 to :2026"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Anonymisation and redaction for EMA Policy 0070 and Health Canada PRCI"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"SOP authoring and investigator training material"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Any single deliverable from the list above, bought on its own"}</span></li></ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Disclosure is deadline-driven and recurring, which is why it works better as a standing arrangement than as a series of emergencies."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#cts-sample"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/?service=Clinical+Trial+Support&package=Custom+and+ongoing&subject=Quote+request%3A+Clinical+Trial+Support+%E2%80%94+Custom+and+ongoing"}>{"Request a quote"}</a> </div> </div> <p className={"smpln rv rv-d2"}>{"Send the protocol and we will run the amendment risk check free — the criteria that will not recruit, the endpoints without a matching estimand, the procedures that map to no objective. Five business days, no charge."}</p> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-guarantee-1av9hzt"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Satisfaction guarantee"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"One promise, with a limit on it and a remedy we name in advance."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"To the current standard, or we rewrite it."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Every document is written to the version of the standard in force on the date of your order, checked against your protocol, and dated to the deadline it has to meet. A document built to a superseded template is ours to fix."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Current versions, checked at order"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"E6(R3) rather than E6(R2), M11 rather than a 2013 template, ISO 14155:2026 rather than the withdrawn 2020 edition. Where a standard moves mid-project, we tell you what it changes."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Traceable to the protocol"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Every statement in a CSR traceable to the protocol, the SAP or the dataset, with deviations from the analysis plan listed rather than quietly absorbed."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Deadlines dated on the order"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Registration within 21 days of first enrolment, results within 12 months of primary completion, lay summaries to the EU CTR timetable. The date goes on the order, not in an email."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"The boundary is in the contract"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We hold no sponsor obligation and accept no transfer of one under 21 CFR 312.52. That is written into the engagement rather than left to be inferred, because an unclear oversight chain is itself an inspection finding."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"05"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Mutual NDA on request"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Signed before you send anything, in both directions, at no cost. Your question, your data and the fact that you are working with us stay confidential either way — and we will sign yours rather than insisting on ours."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-client-stories-djyp7k"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"tcard rv"} id={"cts-quotes"}> <div className={"tcard__top"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"quote__nav"}> <button className={"qbtn"} data-q={"prev"} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"}><path d={"M15 5l-7 7 7 7"} /></svg></button> <button className={"qbtn"} data-q={"next"} aria-label={"Next testimonial"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} /></svg></button> </div> </div>  <div className={"quote__slide"}> <blockquote>{"“The amendment risk check found four eligibility criteria carried over from an earlier study. "}<mark>{"We changed them before ethics submission rather than eight months after it."}</mark>{"”"}</blockquote> <div className={"tcard__foot"}> <div className={"tcard__who"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b><span>{"Principal investigator"}</span></div> <p className={"tcard__org"}>{"Institution to be confirmed"}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"quote__slide"} hidden={true}> <blockquote>{"“"}<mark>{"The statistical analysis plan was written before the database was built"}</mark>{", with the estimand settled first. That is not how our previous trial went.”"}</blockquote> <div className={"tcard__foot"}> <div className={"tcard__who"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b><span>{"Head of clinical development"}</span></div> <p className={"tcard__org"}>{"Company to be confirmed"}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"quote__slide"} hidden={true}> <blockquote>{"“They drafted and filed the results record on our account and put the deadline on the plan. "}<mark>{"We have not missed one since."}</mark>{"”"}</blockquote> <div className={"tcard__foot"}> <div className={"tcard__who"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b><span>{"Research office director"}</span></div> <p className={"tcard__org"}>{"Institution to be confirmed"}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-clinical-trial-support-faq-1ng8kvb"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Clinical trial support FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Eight questions."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"If yours is not here, "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-0"}><span>{"Are you a CRO?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and the distinction is legal rather than presentational. In the United States, 21 CFR 312.3 defines a contract research organisation as a party that assumes one or more sponsor obligations, and 312.52 provides that a CRO which does so is subject to the same regulatory action as a sponsor. We accept no such transfer."}</p><p>{"In India the line is harder still: since 1 April 2025, Chapter VA of the amended New Drugs and Clinical Trials Rules makes CDSCO registration mandatory for any organisation conducting trials or bioequivalence studies on a sponsor’s behalf. We produce documentation, analysis and evidence; you remain the sponsor and hold every obligation."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-1"}><span>{"Then what happens to the parts you do not do?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"They go to a contracted CRO, a site management organisation or your own team, and we work alongside them. Monitoring, site management, patient recruitment, investigational product handling and safety case processing of record all sit there."}</p><p>{"This is a normal division of labour rather than an unusual one. Several substantial firms in this market sell exactly the documentation and evidence scope without trial conduct, and sponsors routinely buy the two separately."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-2"}><span>{"Why does the ICH version matter so much?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Because several of them changed recently and most material in circulation has not caught up. E6(R3) replaced E6(R2), with Annex 1 effective in the EU in July 2025 and Annex 2 from January 2027. M11 became the harmonised protocol standard at Step 4 in November 2025. CONSORT and SPIRIT both moved to 2025 versions, the Declaration of Helsinki was revised in 2024, and GPP 2022 replaced GPP3."}</p><p>{"For device sponsors the sharpest one is ISO 14155: the 2020 edition is withdrawn and the fourth edition was published in March 2026. A clinical investigation plan written to the withdrawn version is a finding waiting to happen."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-3"}><span>{"Can you help with a trial that is already running?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and it is a common point of entry. Amendments, interim reports, DSUR and annual reports, a results record that is approaching or past its deadline, or a CSR for a trial that finished some time ago."}</p><p>{"If the trial is mid-flight the first thing worth doing is usually a disclosure check, because those deadlines run whether or not anybody is watching them, and FDA has moved from pre-notice letters to notices of noncompliance."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-4"}><span>{"Who signs and submits the documents?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"You do. Registry records are drafted and filed on your account under your responsible party; regulatory content is prepared for your signature; the protocol and the CSR carry your name."}</p><p>{"This is not a formality. Obligations that are not transferred in writing remain with the sponsor, and an oversight chain that is unclear about who holds what is itself something inspectors record."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-5"}><span>{"Do you do the statistics, or only the writing?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Both. Sample size and power, randomisation schedule specification, the analysis plan with the estimand framed under E9(R1), and independent analysis against your locked dataset with tables, listings and figures."}</p><p>{"What we do not do is own the clinical database. Database build, validation, lock and custody as the system of record sit with your data management function or your CRO — and we analyse what they lock."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-6"}><span>{"What does the free amendment risk check actually look at?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Eligibility criteria against the population each one excludes; endpoints against whether an estimand exists for them; the schedule of assessments against which procedures map to an objective; and the registration and disclosure obligations the geography creates."}</p><p>{"Those four account for most avoidable amendments. The 2016 Tufts work found 45% of amendments avoidable, and the more recent data shows the count rising rather than falling."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"cts-7"}><span>{"Do you work on device and supplement studies as well as drug trials?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"cts-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes. Device studies are built to ISO 14155:2026, 21 CFR 812 and EU MDR rather than to ICH E6 alone, with the significant-risk determination driving whether a full IDE is needed."}</p><p>{"For supplement and nutraceutical studies the prior question is whether an IND is required, which turns on the claim under study rather than on the product: a structure-function claim generally does not trigger one, a disease claim generally does. We will tell you which side of that line your protocol is on before you design around it."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What comes before and after a trial."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Trial documentation sits between the evidence that justified the study and the publication that reports it. These are the services either side."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"BEFORE THE PROTOCOL"}</b><em>{"the case for the trial"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/discovery-intelligence"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Discovery and intelligence"}</b><span>{"Compound, patent and landscape evidence."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/experimental-design"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Experimental design"}</b><span>{"Design, endpoints and sample size."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"WHILE IT RUNS"}</b><em>{"data and analysis"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/medical-data-collection"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Medical data collection"}</b><span>{"Protocol-driven collection and management."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/biostatistics"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Biostatistics"}</b><span>{"Analysis against a pre-specified plan."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"AFTER IT CLOSES"}</b><em>{"reporting the result"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/regulatory-writing"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Regulatory writing"}</b><span>{"Dossiers, briefs and submission content."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/original-research-article"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Original research article"}</b><span>{"The manuscript, to CONSORT 2025."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading."}</h2> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/nih-public-access-policy-2025/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Policy"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"What funders require of trial results"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Deposit, disclosure and what counts as compliance."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/japan-immediate-open-access/"} data-nav={""}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Policy"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"Where trial reports have to appear"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Immediate access and the publication route."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send the protocol. We will run the amendment risk check free."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"The eligibility criteria that will not recruit, the endpoints with no matching estimand, and the procedures that map to no objective. Five business days, no charge."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
